CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Capsid protein C]: Homodimer. Interacts (via N-terminus) with
CC       host EXOC1 (via C-terminus) (PubMed:19889084, PubMed:23522008); this
CC       interaction results in EXOC1 degradation through the proteasome
CC       degradation pathway (PubMed:23522008). Interacts (via the NLS) with
CC       host KPNA2/Importin alpha-1; this interaction allows the nuclear import
CC       of the capsid protein (By similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01299,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:19889084, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23522008}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Protein prM]: Heterodimer with envelope protein E; each spike
CC       of the immature virion in the ER/Golgi consists of three prM-E
CC       heterodimers. {ECO:0000305|PubMed:9971841}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Small envelope protein M]: Heterotetramer with envelope
CC       protein E, made up of two M-E dimers; in mature virion, prefusion
CC       state. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01299}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Envelope protein E]: Homodimer; in mature virion, prefusion
CC       state (PubMed:23236058). Homotrimer; in mature virion, postfusion state
CC       (PubMed:23236058, PubMed:25355881). Heterotetramer with the small
CC       membrane protein, made up of two M-E dimers; in mature virion,
CC       prefusion state (By similarity). Heterodimer with protein prM; each
CC       spike of the immature virion in the ER/Golgi consists of three prM-E
CC       heterodimers (PubMed:11893341, PubMed:9971841). Interacts with the
CC       peptide pr; this interaction allows the stabilization of the E dimer at
CC       acidic pH (By similarity). Pr remains bound to the particle as long as
CC       the pH is acidic because of electrostatic complementarity, dissociation
CC       of pr occurs at neutral pH upon virus release from the infected cell
CC       (By similarity). Interacts with non-structural protein 1
CC       (PubMed:26562291). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P14336,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:11893341, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23236058,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:25355881, ECO:0000269|PubMed:26562291,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:9971841}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Non-structural protein 1]: Homodimer; Homohexamer when
CC       secreted (PubMed:10364366, PubMed:24594604, PubMed:2827377). Interacts
CC       with envelope protein E (PubMed:26562291).
CC       {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10364366, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24594604,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:26562291, ECO:0000269|PubMed:2827377}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Non-structural protein 2A]: Interacts (via N-terminus) with
CC       serine protease NS3. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P03314}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Serine protease subunit NS2B]: Forms a heterodimer with
CC       serine protease NS3 (PubMed:20042502). May form homooligomers
CC       (PubMed:26728778). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:20042502,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:26728778}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Serine protease NS3]: Forms a heterodimer with NS2B
CC       (PubMed:20042502). Interacts with NS4B (PubMed:16894199). Interacts
CC       with unphosphorylated RNA-directed RNA polymerase NS5; this interaction
CC       stimulates RNA-directed RNA polymerase NS5 guanylyltransferase activity
CC       (PubMed:15917225, PubMed:19850911). Interacts with host SHFL
CC       (PubMed:27974568). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:15917225,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:16894199, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19850911,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:20042502, ECO:0000269|PubMed:27974568}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Non-structural protein 4A]: Interacts with host MAVS; this
CC       interaction inhibits the synthesis of IFN-beta (PubMed:27252539).
CC       Interacts with host SHFL (PubMed:27974568). Interacts with host AUP1;
CC       the interaction occurs in the presence of Dengue virus NS4B and induces
CC       lipophagy which facilitates production of virus progeny particles (By
CC       similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P29991,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:27252539, ECO:0000269|PubMed:27974568}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Non-structural protein 4B]: Interacts with serine protease
CC       NS3 (PubMed:16894199). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:16894199}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [RNA-directed RNA polymerase/Methyltransferase NS5]: Homodimer
CC       (PubMed:26895240). Interacts with host STAT2; this interaction inhibits
CC       the phosphorylation of the latter, and, when all viral proteins are
CC       present (polyprotein), targets STAT2 for degradation (PubMed:19279106).
CC       Interacts with serine protease NS3 (PubMed:15917225, PubMed:19850911).
CC       Interacts (via C-terminus) with host SCRIB (via PDZ3); this interaction
CC       targets NS5 to the cell membrane periphery and nucleus, thereby
CC       allowing efficient host nuclear STAT1 inhibition (By similarity).
CC       Interacts with host PAF1 complex; the interaction may prevent the
CC       recruitment of the PAF1 complex to interferon-responsive genes, and
CC       thus reduces the immune response (By similarity).
CC       {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P09866, ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01299,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:15917225, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19279106,
CC       ECO:0000269|PubMed:19850911, ECO:0000269|PubMed:26895240}.
