CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Capsid protein C]: Homodimer (By similarity). Interacts (via
CC       the NLS) with host KPNA2/Importin alpha-1; this interaction allows the
CC       nuclear import of the capsid protein (By similarity).
CC       {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P14336, ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01299}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Protein prM]: Heterodimer with envelope protein E; each spike
CC       of the immature virion in the ER/Golgi consists of three prM-E
CC       heterodimers. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P14336}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Small envelope protein M]: Heterotetramer with envelope
CC       protein E, made up of two M-E dimers; in mature virion, prefusion
CC       state. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01299}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Envelope protein E]: Homodimer; in mature virion, prefusion
CC       state (By similarity). Homotrimer; in mature virion, postfusion state
CC       (By similarity). Heterotetramer with the small membrane protein, made
CC       up of two M-E dimers; in mature virion, prefusion state (By
CC       similarity). Heterodimer with protein prM; each spike of the immature
CC       virion in the ER/Golgi consists of three prM-E heterodimers (By
CC       similarity). Interacts with the peptide pr; this interaction allows the
CC       stabilization of the E dimer at acidic pH (By similarity). Pr remains
CC       bound to the particle as long as the pH is acidic because of
CC       electrostatic complementarity, dissociation of pr occurs at neutral pH
CC       upon virus release from the infected cell (By similarity). Interacts
CC       with non-structural protein 1 (By similarity).
CC       {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P07720, ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P14336,
CC       ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P17763, ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01299}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Non-structural protein 1]: Homodimer; Homohexamer when
CC       secreted. Interacts with envelope protein E.
CC       {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P17763}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Non-structural protein 2A]: Interacts (via N-terminus) with
CC       serine protease NS3. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P03314}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Serine protease subunit NS2B]: Forms a heterodimer with
CC       serine protease NS3 (By similarity). May form homooligomers (By
CC       similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P17763}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Serine protease/helicase NS3]: Forms a heterodimer with NS2B
CC       (By similarity). Interacts with non-structural protein 2A (via N-
CC       terminus) (By similarity). Interacts with NS4B (By similarity).
CC       Interacts with unphosphorylated RNA-directed RNA polymerase NS5; this
CC       interaction stimulates RNA-directed RNA polymerase NS5
CC       guanylyltransferase activity (By similarity).
CC       {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P17763}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [Non-structural protein 4B]: Interacts with serine protease
CC       NS3 (By similarity). Interacts with NS1 (By similarity).
CC       {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P17763}.
CC   -!- SUBUNIT: [RNA-directed RNA polymerase/Methyltransferase NS5]: Homodimer
CC       (By similarity). Interacts with host STAT2; this interaction inhibits
CC       the phosphorylation of the latter, and, when all viral proteins are
CC       present (polyprotein), targets STAT2 for degradation (By similarity).
CC       Interacts with serine protease NS3 (By similarity). Interacts (via C-
CC       terminus) with host SCRIB (via PDZ3); this interaction targets NS5 to
CC       the cell membrane periphery and nucleus, thereby allowing efficient
CC       host nuclear STAT1 inhibition (By similarity).
CC       {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P17763, ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01299}.
